    core:proteinSubcellularLocationText "Apical cell membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12519745, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12529365, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1284548, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15247260, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15716351, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17462998, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19398555, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19621064, ECO:0000269|PubMed:20008117, ECO:0000269|PubMed:22207244, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28130590}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000269|Ref.57}. Early endosome membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:19398555, ECO:0000269|PubMed:20008117}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000269|Ref.57}. Cell membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:10792060, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11524016, ECO:0000269|PubMed:11707463, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12588899, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15010471, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17036051, ECO:0000269|PubMed:1712898, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17182731, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19019741, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19398555, ECO:0000269|PubMed:21884936, ECO:0000269|PubMed:22178883, ECO:0000269|PubMed:25330774, ECO:0000269|PubMed:26846474, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28001373, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28067262, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28087700, ECO:0000269|PubMed:28130590, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9804160, ECO:0000305|PubMed:8910473}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000269|Ref.57}. Recycling endosome membrane {ECO:0000305|PubMed:17462998}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000269|Ref.57}. Endoplasmic reticulum membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11707463, ECO:0000269|PubMed:25330774}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000269|Ref.57}. Nucleus {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P34158}. Note=The channel is internalized from the cell surface into an endosomal recycling compartment, from where it is recycled to the cell membrane (PubMed:17462998, PubMed:19398555, PubMed:20008117). In the oviduct and bronchus, detected on the apical side of epithelial cells, but not associated with cilia (PubMed:22207244). In Sertoli cells, a processed product is detected in the nucleus (By similarity). ER stress induces GORASP2-mediated unconventional (ER/Golgi-independent) trafficking of core-glycosylated CFTR to cell membrane (PubMed:21884936). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P34158, ECO:0000269|PubMed:19398555, ECO:0000269|PubMed:20008117, ECO:0000269|PubMed:21884936, ECO:0000269|PubMed:22207244, ECO:0000305|PubMed:17462998}." .

uniprot:Q13464 a core:Protein,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Protein Q13464" ;
    core:domainOrderText "INTERPRO:IPR000719 > INTERPRO:IPR000961 > INTERPRO:IPR011072 > INTERPRO:IPR037310 > INTERPRO:IPR015008 > INTERPRO:IPR001849 > INTERPRO:IPR057529 > INTERPRO:IPR002219" ;
    core:proteinSubcellularLocationText "Cytoplasm {ECO:0000269|PubMed:8617235}. Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton, microtubule organizing center, centrosome, centriole {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P70335}. Golgi apparatus membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12773565}; Peripheral membrane protein {ECO:0000269|PubMed:12773565}. Cell projection, bleb {ECO:0000269|PubMed:18694941}. Cytoplasm, cytoskeleton {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P70335}. Cell membrane {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P70335}. Cell projection, lamellipodium {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P70335}. Cell projection, ruffle {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P70335}. Note=A small proportion is associated with Golgi membranes (PubMed:12773565). Associated with the mother centriole and an intercentriolar linker (By similarity). Colocalizes with ITGB1BP1 and ITGB1 at the cell membrane predominantly in lamellipodia and membrane ruffles, but also in retraction fibers (By similarity). Localizes at the cell membrane in an ITGB1BP1-dependent manner (By similarity). {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P70335, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12773565}." .

uniprot:Q13936 a core:Protein,
        owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "Protein Q13936" ;
    core:domainOrderText "INTERPRO:IPR005821 > INTERPRO:IPR005821 > INTERPRO:IPR005821 > INTERPRO:IPR005821 > INTERPRO:IPR005821 > INTERPRO:IPR031649 > INTERPRO:IPR014873 > INTERPRO:IPR031688" ;
    core:proteinSubcellularLocationText "Cell membrane {ECO:0000269|PubMed:11741969, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12176756, ECO:0000269|PubMed:12181424, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15454078, ECO:0000269|PubMed:15863612, ECO:0000269|PubMed:16299511, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17071743, ECO:0000269|PubMed:17224476, ECO:0000269|PubMed:20953164, ECO:0000269|PubMed:24728418, ECO:0000269|PubMed:26253506, ECO:0000269|PubMed:27218670, ECO:0000269|PubMed:29078335, ECO:0000269|PubMed:29742403, ECO:0000269|PubMed:7737988, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8099908, ECO:0000269|PubMed:8392192, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9013606, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9087614, ECO:0000269|PubMed:9607315}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000305}. Cell membrane, sarcolemma {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15381}; Multi-pass membrane protein {ECO:0000305}. Perikaryon {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P22002}. Postsynaptic density membrane {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P22002}. Cell projection, dendrite {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P22002}. Cell membrane, sarcolemma, T-tubule {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:Q01815}. Note=Colocalizes with ryanodine receptors in distinct clusters at the junctional membrane, where the sarcolemma and the sarcoplasmic reticulum are in close contact. The interaction between RRAD and CACNB2 promotes the expression of CACNA1C at the cell membrane. {ECO:0000250|UniProtKB:P15381}." .

